  "metadata": {
    "title": "Pairwise Teams and Reverse Work Relations",
    "description": "Recover individual rates from team-pair information and reciprocal equations.",
    "teachingApproach": "Teach the pairwise identity before algebra: AB + BC + AC counts each worker twice. Use it to find ABC, then subtract a pair to isolate one worker. Move into relative-time equations and together-time equations with fixed differences or ratios, always rejecting impossible negative times.",
    "targetDurationMinutes": 31,
    "sourceScope": "R.S. Aggarwal, Quantitative Aptitude for Competitive Examinations, Chapter 17, Time and Work. Approved scope: Teach pairwise-rate identities. From AB, BC and AC rates, add them to get twice the ABC rate, then subtract a pair to recover an individual. Cover finding the fastest worker, an individual when A equals the combined rate of B and C, and reverse relations such as B taking a multiple of the time taken by A+C. Include simple reciprocal equations where a together-time and a difference or ratio between individual times determine the workers."
  },
